 and make a  film this film it was a wide open  program of asking people to let us film  aspects of that private life that they  wanted filmed this requires an awful lot  of energy all the way through the tongue  Ricky wanted to make double system  equipment so that anyone could make a  documentary film that they were  interested in making I came to MIT to  work on super ade and I couldn't  understand why you couldn't sync sound  recording that you made on a tape  recorder with the film that came out of  a super 8 film camera MIT had the answer  [Music]  another room the film/video section  became the venue for artists to come to  and want to screen their films for our  audience the Monday night screenings  where I was open to the public  Mary Jane Dougherty who made the  funniest films that were released I mean  she really had a wonderful sense of  humor this is an experimental  astrophysics laboratory heavy double  stars that the rotate around each other  you know  garetty waves and this is what ray is  looking for  I think the move to the Media Lab it was  by choice but it was also sort of  self-evident that we needed to go there  if we were going to invent some of the  new technologies and the new approaches  to video and that's of course what MIT  is all about it's about invention and  moving on to the new in terms of film  video it was very clear to me and to a  few others at the section at that time  that computers were going to totally  change how we edited  [Music]  Ricci himself I think was not so  interested in staying long-term at MIT  he wanted to go off and make more of the  type of movies he'd been talking about  using the video 8 technology and just  see what you would make if you hung out  on the streets of Paris one of the  really strong memories I have of the  film section in the film video section  and even my groups here the interactive  cinema group are all the fantastic  people who went through it really was  remarkable particularly in the early  days I think there wasn't anything like  that in the country there are many very  accomplished filmmakers who came out of  the film section Ross McElwee robb maus  Steve Asher  Burnie Schneider Alex Anthony Mary Jane  Dorothy very strong and and just many  more moving through into the days of the  Media Lab as well yeah  very influential  [Music]  you

